tic state legislator, has raised only about $22,000 and had $356 on hand, with no outside support on either side.\n\nEvery major expert rater calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets put Democratic odds at just one to three percent. The only notable friction is criticism of Hageman and her House successor for skipping PBS debates, which is unlikely to matter in a state this red. The forecast expects a Republican win by roughly nineteen points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -17.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0045, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0194, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0012, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0022, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0042, "margin": -19.0}]}